  m_Name: ButterflyValveData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  engineName: Butterfly Valve
  engineDescription: "A Butterfly Valve is a quarter-turn flow control valve used
    to regulate, isolate, or stop the flow of liquids and gases in piping systems.
    Its main components are the valve body, disc, stem, actuator or handle, and sealing
    seat. During operation, the disc rotates through 90 degrees to either allow,
    restrict, or completely stop fluid flow, providing quick and efficient flow control
    with minimal pressure loss. \nButterfly valves are widely used in water treatment
    plants, HVAC systems, chemical processing, oil and gas industries, fire protection
    systems, and power plants. From an engineering perspective, understanding valve
    sizing, pressure drop, sealing performance, flow characteristics, actuator selection,
    and maintenance is essential for ensuring reliable, efficient, and long-lasting
    fluid control."
  engineCategory: Engineering
